{"spec_element": "ensures",
 "proof_obligation": "bridge",
 "diagnosis": "SkippingLemma's postcondition claims all indices from j up to and including j+a[j] are nonzero. But the precondition only guarantees a[j+a[j]] >= a[j]-a[j] = 0, so a[j+a[j]] can be zero while satisfying the precondition. The loop invariant only covers indices strictly less than i, and at exit i can equal j+a[j], so the postcondition is too strong by one and fails."}

